/* book exam traps: Gain is δⁿ, not nδ: 10 dynodes with δ = 4 give 1,048,576, not 40. | Dark current is multiplied by the same gain, so a PMT shows dark counts; cooling the photocathode reduces them. | A phototube has no gain; only the PMT has dynodes. Do not use the two names interchangeably. | In a scintillation counter the scintillator makes light; the PMT only multiplies photoelectrons. A gamma ray is not counted directly by the PMT. | Pulse height gives energy, pulse count rate gives intensity. Do not use count rate to identify the isotope energy. */
