/* book exam traps: Absorbance is logarithmic. Doubling concentration doubles A only inside the linear range; it does not double transmittance. | A = ε c l needs c in mol/L and l in cm. Convert a path length given in mm or a concentration given in mmol/L before dividing. | Dark current is not a light signal. It adds an offset, so zero or subtract it correctly and do not treat it as absorbance. | Responsivity in A/W is wavelength dependent. A value quoted at 850 nm cannot be used at 1550 nm without a new calibration. | An LDR is slow and nonlinear; a photovoltaic cell is a power source. Neither is a good choice for fast, precise spectrophotometry. */
